       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg per day is 5 times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day for adults. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. It's also a possible 10-fold error, since the usual starting dose is 50 mg and 100 mg is common.\n\nCan you confirm the intended dose? These are typical options:\n- **Starting dose:** 25\u201350 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Usual maintenance dose:** 50\u2013200 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg per day.\n\nOnce you give me a dose at or below 200 mg/day, I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1000 mg, please talk with pharmacy or the attending first. I can't enter a dose above the labeled maximum."
